    {
      "title": "West Bengal govt in talks with farmers to acquire 997 acres in Singur: CM",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/west-bengal-govt-in-talks-with-farmers-to-acquire-997-acres-in-singur-cm-126112200687_1.html",
      "description": "West Bengal Chief Minister Suvendu Adhikari on Sunday said his government was in talks with farmers to acquire 997 acres of land in Singur in Hooghly district, a day after Union Minister Sukanta Majumdar announced Ashok Leyland would set up a truck manufacturing plant there.\nSingur was the site of Tata Motors' Nano small-car factory, for which the then Left Front government acquired around 997 acres in 2006. The acquisition triggered a prolonged farmers' agitation led by Mamata Banerjee, following which Tata Motors moved the project to Sanand in Gujarat in 2008.\nIn August 2016, the Supreme Court quashed the land acquisition and ordered that the land be returned to the farmers.\n\"The West Bengal Industrial Development Corporation (WBIDC) had been tasked with acquiring the 997 acres, and negotiations with farmers were underway to purchase the land at a reasonable rate,\" Adhikari told reporters.\nHe said the government would \"do something\" with the land, without mentioning Ashok Leyland",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-22T17:21:06"
    }
